# DTF tier manifest: push-sync-oci-and-plugin-metadata
#   (artifact-keeper 1.12.0 push replication fixes: #4790, #4916)
# Profile-set: filesystem + a real second Artifact Keeper instance
# (peer.second-instance: `peer-backend` with its own `peer-db`, same image,
# published on 127.0.0.1:${TRIVY_PORT}). A is `backend`; B is the push peer
# A's sync worker (10 s tick) delivers to over the slot's compose network.
# Two backends and two databases: run it alone on a loaded host.
#
# Why a tier of its own and not more cases in push-sync-native-formats: that
# tier is in the 1.11.x gate and both fixes are 1.12.0-only (red on 1.11.13).
#
# THE PEER
# As in push-sync-native-formats: a `*`-scoped API key minted on B, B
# registered on A and set online in A's DB, hosted docker, maven and generic
# repositories subscribed in push mode; the same keys exist on B.
#
# RED image: 1.11.13 (neither #4850 nor #4981 is on the 1.11 line; checked
# with git merge-base --is-ancestor). GREEN: main (sha-2bdf092 or later).
#
# CONTROLS (pass on every image)
#   a generic upload on A reaches B (row, sha256, served bytes); the image
#   and the index pushed with curl over /v2 pull back from A; a Maven jar
#   and its pom uploaded to A reach B.
#
# FIX CASES (RED on 1.11.13: nothing of them reaches B)
#   #4790 an OCI image (config + two layers) pushed to a hosted docker
#     repository reaches B: the manifest by tag with A's digest, by digest,
#     and every blob it references with its digest. An image index over two
#     child manifests reaches B with both children and their blobs.
#   #4916 (item 4) a group-level plugin-prefix maven-metadata.xml
#     (<plugins>) uploaded to A reaches B, and B merges it into the mapping
#     it already held: B's own prefix stays, A's prefixes are added.
#   The other #4916 items (orphaned label objects, pre-#4889 empty rows,
#   two-way label moves) are covered by the backend's tests named in the PR.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: a few dozen authenticated calls on A and B.
# UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS=true: the peer endpoint goes through
# validate_outbound_url and B sits on a private compose address.
COVERS="4790 4916"
PROFILES="storage.filesystem peer.second-instance"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
